  "changes": [
    "After exact Gateway and local usage settlement, rejected compaction responses record a finite fixed diagnostic event bound to original call/run/generation and input/frontier hashes. Response text/excerpts/tool names/exception messages are never persisted.",
    "Record response SHA256, actual UTF8 bytes, original summary byte cap, allowlisted finish class, tool count, identity-match booleans and fixed rejection predicates. Source-bound validation failure records its fixed checkpoint stage and preserves the original exception.",
    "Reduce compaction max_output_tokens to min(self.output_limit,max(1,summary_bytes//4)); preserve the original dynamic summary-byte cap and final UTF8 byte validator. The ratio is a conservative estimate, not a byte guarantee.",
    "Feedback separates actual remaining cumulative tokens from current_request_token_allowance. Both use existing input-framing accounting and grant no new execution authority."
  ],
